                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "LGTM"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "previously this returned nullopt. Did something change so now it shouldn't?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/utils.cpp",
                    "line": 195,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Now it returns `true` which is mapped to `ret` on the right side of the diff on line 312.\nWhich is `nullopt` in the caller function.\n\n```\nstd::optional<std::string> ret = std::nullopt;\n\n...\n\nif (templateCharReplaceLoop(strPtr, interface, ret, value))\n{\n    return ret;\n}\n```\n\nWhen extracting a function, any `return` inside that now called function has to be mapped to a `return` in the new caller function as well.\n\nI'm using `true` to cause the `return ret;` in the calling function and `false` to continue the normal control flow."
                }
            ],
